OL,3,AHuw Edwards gives first interviews
OL,4,Asince child abuse image conviction
OL,5,
OL,6,FDisgraced former BBC News presenter Huw
OL,7,FEdwards has given his first interviews
OL,8,Fsince being convicted in 2024 for
OL,9,Fmaking indecent images of children.
OL,11,FEdwards is seen saying he believes
OL,12,F"silence is toxic" in a clip of a
OL,13,Fpodcast released by the Observer
OL,14,Fnewspaper, and he has also been
OL,15,Finterviewed for a Channel 4
OL,16,Fdocumentary.
OL,23,APub: 26-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG12/19
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,163,160,200,105,0,100
PN,11913
SC,0013
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1795731554
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AHuw Edwards gives first interviews
OL,4,Asince child abuse image conviction
OL,5,
OL,6,FA government minister, Anna Turley,
OL,7,Ftold LBC she was "deeply uncomfortable"
OL,8,Fwith the interviews, and that "for too
OL,9,Flong, so many of these people in the
OL,10,Fpublic eye have been able to have a
OL,11,Fsort of free pass".
OL,13,FChannel 4 has defended the documentary.
OL,14,FA spokesperson told the BBC that a
OL,15,F"highly experienced director" holds
OL,16,FEdwards to account with "no questions
OL,17,Foff limits, revealing his account of
OL,18,Fwhat led to his offending and very
OL,19,Fpublic downfall".
OL,23,APub: 26-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/19
